' F19 -- Results.
' HERO FIGURE (intended). Chapter 6 (Evaluation).
'
' ############################################################################
' # THIS IS A SCAFFOLD. IT CONTAINS NO RESULTS AND MUST NOT BE SUBMITTED     #
' # AS-IS. No evaluation run exists yet: `eval_runs` was never applied to    #
' # production, and no local scorecard has been recorded. Inventing numbers  #
' # here would be fabrication, so the slots are deliberately empty.          #
' #                                                                          #
' # To complete it: run `python -m backend.eval.run_eval`, take the          #
' # Scorecard, and fill the four metric rows plus the band thresholds.       #
' ############################################################################
@startuml f19-results-scaffold
!include _style.iuml

title Results — SCAFFOLD, no data recorded yet

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

rectangle "**⚠  NO EVALUATION HAS BEEN RUN**\nEvery value below is a placeholder.\nRun backend/eval/run_eval.py and fill them in." as WARN #BFBFBF

rectangle "**Scorecard** — one row per metric" as CARD #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "Quiz key accuracy\n----\nscore:  ______\nband:   ______\nn cases: ______\nverdict: ______" as M1
  rectangle "Tutor faithfulness\n----\nscore:  ______\nband:   ______\nn cases: ______\nverdict: ______" as M2
  rectangle "Retrieval precision@k\n----\nscore:  ______\nband:   ______\nk = 5 (lecture) / 6 (course)\nverdict: ______" as M3
  rectangle "Synthesis quality (LLM judge)\n----\nscore:  ______\nband:   ______\nn cases: ______\nverdict: ______" as M4
}

rectangle "**Run metadata**\n----\ncommit:      ______\npipeline:     Live / Fake\nmodel(s):     ______\ndate:         ______\noverall:      PASS / FAIL" as META #F2F2F2

WARN --> CARD
CARD --> META

note right of CARD
  These four metrics are the ones the existing
  harness actually computes (see F18). Do not add
  a fifth row without adding a scorer for it —
  a metric with no code behind it is the same
  class of error as the README claims audited in
  the honesty ledger.
end note

note bottom of META
  **Claims this figure can support once filled:**
  pipeline output quality against curated golden sets,
  measured reproducibly at a known commit.

  **Claims it can NEVER support, however good the numbers:**
  that students learned more. There is no controlled study,
  no comparison group, and `learning_events` retention
  defaults to 0 (never archive) with no analysis pipeline
  behind it. Say so explicitly rather than letting a reader
  infer a learning-outcomes claim from a quality metric.
end note

legend bottom
  Placeholder figure, tracked deliberately so the gap is visible rather than forgotten.
  Replace before submission or remove the figure and its reference from Chapter 6.
endlegend

@enduml
